Task: Direction-aware document generation (Phase 2 of asyncapi-cdc-direction_20261018)

Summary: Reworked AsyncApiDoc.toChannelItem/toMessage to filter publish/
subscribe oneOf membership by each channel's direction. A ChannelItem
omits the publish (or subscribe) operation entirely (Option.map, not an
empty oneOf) when no registered channel on that topic qualifies.

Note: toMessage's withCdcNote parameter and the CDC-description wiring
(Phase 3's planned scope) were implemented together with this phase's
direction filtering, since both touch the exact same toMessage/
toChannelItem call sites and splitting them would have meant writing
the publish-channel-filtering logic twice. Phase 3's own tests will
likely pass immediately against this commit - that's expected, not a
shortcut, and will be verified/documented there.

Files:
- modules/purekafka/src/main/scala/purekafka/docs/AsyncApiDoc.scala (reworked)
- modules/purekafka/src/test/scala/purekafka/docs/AsyncApiDocSuite.scala (3 new tests)

TDD: Red confirmed (3 new tests failed against the old always-both
